## 1. R Package: InferMultiModal

The `InferMultiModal/` directory contains the R package implementing the proposed methodology.

The package provides functions for:

- Model estimation;
- Prediction;
- Hypothesis Testing of Idiosyncratic Residual Effects;
- Hypothesis Testing of Modality-shared and Modality-specific Factor Effects.

Detailed documentation of the package functions is available in the `man/` directory.

## 2. Simulation Studies

The `simulation/` directory contains the scripts for conducting simulation experiments and reproducing the corresponding figures and tables.

### 2.1 Simulation Settings

Five simulation settings are considered:

- **Main Setting:** The primary simulation scenario provided in the main manuscript.
- **No-Common-Component Setting:** A scenario without the common component (P1).
- **Only-Common-Component Setting:** A scenario in which only the common component is present (P2).
- **Weak Setting:** A scenario with weaker signals.
- **Lower-Noise Setting:** A scenario with a lower noise level.

The corresponding simulation data are organized in separate subdirectories under `Data/Simulation/`.

### 2.2 Sensitivity Analysis

Sensitivity analyses are conducted under the main simulation setting to investigate the robustness of the proposed method to latent dimension misspecification.

The corresponding scripts are located in:

```text
simulation/Replication_code/MainSetting/R_sensitivity/
```

The sensitivity analysis data and results are associated with the main simulation setting.

### 2.3 Replication Code

The `simulation/Replication_code/` directory contains the R scripts for reproducing the simulation experiments under different settings.

Each subdirectory corresponds to a particular simulation scenario and contains the scripts required to conduct the corresponding experiments.

### 2.4 Figures and Tables

The `simulation/Fig_Tab_Code/` directory contains the R scripts used to generate the figures and tables reported in the main paper and supplementary materials.

The script names indicate the corresponding figure or table numbers.

## 3. Alternative Methods 

The `alternative/` directory contains the implementations of alternative methods used for comparison with the proposed approach.

The main files include:

- `beta_li.R`: Our implementation of the integrative factor regression method proposed by Li and Li (2022).
- `beta_fan.R`: An adapted and wrapped version of the publicly available implementation of the method proposed by Fan et al. (2024).
- `joint_func.R`: Functions for joint estimation.

## 4. Real Data Analysis

The `realdata/` directory contains the scripts for the real data analyses. The corresponding datasets are stored in `Data/RealData/`, with raw and processed data organized separately.

The real data analyses are based on two TCGA lung cancer cohorts: lung adenocarcinoma (LUAD) and lung squamous cell carcinoma (LUSC). Four types of molecular data are considered: mRNA expression, DNA methylation, copy number alteration (CNA), and protein expression. The clinical outcome is the pre-bronchodilator FEV1 percentage of predicted value.

The analysis scripts are divided into two groups.

### 4.1 Full-Sample Analysis

The `Full_Sample_Analysis/` directory contains scripts for analyses based on the full sample.

- `Whole_Sample.R`: Performs the real data analysis using the full sample.
- `Fig5.R`: Generates Figure 5 based on the full-sample analysis results.
- `Tab2.R`: Generates Table 2 based on the full-sample analysis results.
- `Realdataxlsx.R`: Generates Realdata.xlsx, which contains the estimated parameters and hypothesis testing results.

### 4.2 Resampling Analysis

The `Resampling_Analysis/` directory contains scripts for evaluating prediction performance and the stability of the analysis results through resampling.

- `Prediction_Stability.R`: Conducts resampling analyses based on a 20:1 training-test split to evaluate prediction performance and the stability of the results.
- `averageError_and_jaccard.R`: Calculates the average estimation error and Jaccard index based on the resampling results, quantifying estimation accuracy and variable selection stability, respectively.

## 5. Data Availability

### 5.1 Data Sources

The original LUAD and LUSC data are publicly available through [cBioPortal](https://www.cbioportal.org/). The corresponding TCGA studies are [LUAD](https://www.cbioportal.org/study/summary?id=luad_tcga) and [LUSC](https://www.cbioportal.org/study/summary?id=lusc_tcga).

The downloaded raw data are stored in `Data/RealData/RawData/`. The processed datasets used in the analyses are provided in `Data/RealData/ProcessedData/`.

### 5.2 Data Preprocessing

The preprocessing scripts are provided in the `realdata/` directory. They document the procedures for extracting the clinical outcome, processing the molecular data, matching samples across data types, and constructing the final analysis datasets from the downloaded raw data.

### 5.3 Processed Data Structure

The processed real data are stored in an RData file as a data frame named `Lung_df`, which combines the LUAD and LUSC cohorts. The dataset contains 241 observations and 1,995 variables, including one clinical outcome and 1,994 molecular features from four data modalities.

The variables are organized as follows:

| Variables (Number) | Description |
|---|---|
| `FEV1_PERCENT_REF_PREBRONCHOLIATOR` (1) | Pre-bronchodilator FEV1 percentage of predicted value (clinical outcome) |
| mRNA expression (300) | Selected mRNA expression features |
| DNA methylation (300) | Selected DNA methylation features |
| Copy number alteration (CNA) (300) | Selected CNA features |
| Protein expression (194) | Protein expression features |
| **Total (1,095)** | |

Each row corresponds to a TCGA sample, with sample identifiers provided as row names. The processed dataset serves as the input for the real-data analyses.

